  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>ticket_triage - extracts structured fields from each helpdesk ticket with the LangExtract service and routes
the critical tickets.
Needs: the LangExtract service on http://localhost:8765 (qwen2.5:7b) and the helpdesk.tickets table in the
pgvector kit's genai database.

1. tbl-tickets: Table input on connection genai: ticket_id, ticket_text FROM helpdesk.tickets WHERE
   processed = 0, oldest first.
2. js-request: Modified JavaScript value builds request_json: the ticket text, the prompt, one worked
   example with the classes issue_type, system, error_code, urgency and user, model_id ${LX_MODEL},
   max_char_buffer 1200, extraction_passes 2.
3. rest-extract: REST client, POST http://localhost:8765/extract, body request_json, result response_json.
4. json-extractions: JSON input on response_json: class, text, start, end from $.extractions[*], one row per
   extraction.
5. sv-pivot: Select values keeps ticket_id, class, text.
6. dnorm-tickets: Row denormaliser, key class, group ticket_id: issue_type, affected_system (system),
   urgency, submitter (user), error_code.
7. flt-critical: Filter rows urgency = Critical; TRUE to critical, FALSE to others.
8. critical, others: Dummy (do nothing) steps that end the two branches.

Parameters: LX_MODEL qwen2.5:7b; PG_HOST localhost, PG_PORT 5433, PG_DATABASE genai, PG_USER
genai, PG_PASSWORD genai.
Shipped data: 6 tickets; 32 extractions, 6 ticket rows, 2 critical (T-1002, T-1004) and 4 others on the course
PC.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>626</width>
      <heigth>422</heigth>
